  "text": "module apbslave #(\n\tparameter\tC_APB_ADDR_WIDTH = 12,\n\tparameter\tC_APB_DATA_WIDTH = 32,\n\tlocalparam\tAW = C_APB_ADDR_WIDTH,\n\tlocalparam\tDW = C_APB_DATA_WIDTH,\n\tlocalparam\tAPBLSB = $clog2(C_APB_DATA_WIDTH)-3\n) (\n\tinput\twire\t\t\tPCLK, PRESETn,\n\tinput\twire\t\t\tPSEL,\n\tinput\twire\t\t\tPENABLE,\n\toutput\treg\t\t\tPREADY,\n\tinput\twire\t[AW-1:0]\tPADDR,\n\tinput\twire\t\t\tPWRITE,\n\tinput\twire\t[DW-1:0]\tPWDATA,\n\tinput\twire\t[DW/8-1:0]\tPWSTRB,\n\tinput\twire\t[2:0]\t\tPPROT,\n\toutput\treg\t[DW-1:0]\tPRDATA,\n\toutput\twire\t\t\tPSLVERR\n);\n\n\treg\t[AW-1:0]\tADDR;\n\treg\t[DW/8-1:0]\tWSTRB;\n\treg\t[DW-1:0]\tDATA;\n\treg\tSTATE;\n\treg\t[DW-1:0]\tOLD_DATA;\n\n\tinitial begin\n\t\tSTATE = 2'b00;\n\t\tPREADY = 1'b0;\n\t\tPSLVERR = 1'b0;\n\t\tPRDATA = 0;\n\tend\n\n\talways @(posedge PCLK or negedge PRESETn) begin\n\t\tif (!PRESETn) begin\n\t\t\tSTATE <= 2'b00;\n\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\tPSLVERR <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\tPRDATA <= 0;\n\t\t\tADDR <= 0;\n\t\t\tWSTRB <= 0;\n\t\t\tDATA <= 0;\n\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\tcase (STATE)\n\t\t\t\t2'b00: begin // IDLE\n\t\t\t\t\tif (PSEL && PENABLE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\tADDR <= PADDR;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tWSTRB <= PWSTRB;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tDATA <= PWDATA;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tSTATE <= 2'b01;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t\t2'b01: begin // ACTIVE\n\t\t\t\t\tif (PSEL && PENABLE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// Read or Write\n\t\t\t\t\t\tif (!PWRITE) begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// Read: Data is already in DATA from previous cycle\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tPRDATA <= DATA;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t// Write: Update internal data\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDATA <= PWDATA;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// For standard APB, we assert ready immediately on the second cycle\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// unless there is a specific latency requirement not mentioned.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// The prompt says \"complete each access by asserting PREADY\".\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// In a 1-cycle latency slave, we assert ready in the next cycle after setup.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// Since we are in the ACTIVE state (cycle 2 of access), we assert ready now.\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPSLVERR <= 1'b0; // PSLVERR stays low for in-range accesses as per prompt\n\t\t\t\t\tend else begin\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// If PSEL or PENABLE goes low while in ACTIVE, we must de-assert ready\n\t\t\t\t\t\t// and wait for the next setup.\n\t\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b0;\n\t\t\t\t\t\tSTATE <= 2'b00;\n\t\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\tend\n\n\t\t\t\tdefault: begin\n\t\t\t\t\tPREADY <= 1'b1;\n\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\tendcase\n\t\tend\n\tend\n\nendmodule<|im_end|>\n<|endoftext|>",
